            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "12cc86e3b7db2203e8d3658d86db0b845acfee191f034ff4e8a410725ff50470",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-12cc86e3b7db-0002-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Robbins, petitioners argue that punitive damages are available against governmental entities because Title\u202fII is silent and thus permits an unlimited punitive\u2011damages remedy."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States, as amicus curiae (Gregory G. Garre)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "12cc86e3b7db2203e8d3658d86db0b845acfee191f034ff4e8a410725ff50470",
