          {
            "document_hash": "12cc86e3b7db2203e8d3658d86db0b845acfee191f034ff4e8a410725ff50470",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-12cc86e3b7db-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court notes that Congress intended the same remedies for states as for private entities, and that punitive damages serve a deterrent purpose."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "12cc86e3b7db2203e8d3658d86db0b845acfee191f034ff4e8a410725ff50470",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-12cc86e3b7db-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court also states that policies are not served by immunizing defendants from punitive damages under a Newport rationale."
      }
